Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Current Build Host Pilot P0 Requirements Analysis

@ [analysis_uuid] 56da67e4-323d-4878-9a66-05e0762a5948
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] cd4a7cf3-dfd8-4615-bd14-d2644bc7420c

& [RequiredOutcome]
  + establish a current-build execution surface on EVO-X2 and measure deterministic governed replay through current Cantor artifacts

& [NecessaryConditions]
  + exact published source lineage fresh local release build closed package membership remote host and root identity preflight staged nonoverwriting install pre/post hashes independent replay verification bounded receipt retrieval protected-root conservation and idle closure

& [TruthConditions]
  + installed means exact manifest bytes exist at the new root; portable means those bytes execute the declared replay successfully; deterministic means two fresh outputs are byte-identical
  + none of those meanings implies build autonomy generative quality provider correctness production trust or permission to edit source

& [Sequencing]
  + source publication then formation publication then implementation tests then live deployment then evidence-bound completion; any failed boundary stops the successor phase

& [Finding]
  + P0 should prove a small executable bridge first and use its evidence to define a later plan-only build contract rather than combining deployment and self-work mutation
